  "homeActivities": [
    {
      "text": "Activity 1 — The waterproof test\nTake four cups. Stretch a different material over the top of each one and hold it with a rubber band: kitchen tissue, a piece of plastic bag, a\npiece of cotton cloth, aluminium foil. Let him predict first — write down his guesses. Then spoon a little water onto each. The plastic and\nthe foil keep the water out. The tissue and the cloth let it through. Now compare: which predictions were right?\nActivity 2 — Twist, stretch, squash, bend\nLine up a piece of dough, a rubber band, a sponge, a metal spoon, a paper straw and a stone. Try each of the four actions on each item.\nWhich materials change shape? Which refuse?\nwood metal plastic glass fabric paper\nhard, floats shiny, cold light, waterproof see-through soft, bendy thin, tears\nSix materials to find in one room. How many can he point at in two minutes?\n",
      "safety": "An adult stays with the child for every activity. No glass, no sockets, no flames, and nothing small enough to swallow is left with a child\nalone. Water activities are done in a bowl or the sink, never near electrical items.",
      "pages": [
        12,
